lessons.notes:
## Colors

```css
color: rebeccapurple;              /* named */
color: #ff6600;  color: #f60;      /* hex (short form) */
color: rgb(255 102 0);             /* modern space syntax */
color: rgb(255 102 0 / 50%);       /* with transparency */
color: hsl(24 100% 50%);           /* hue saturation lightness */
background: linear-gradient(to right, #e34c26, #f0a500);
```

Check **contrast**: normal text needs a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 with its background (WCAG AA).

## Custom properties

```css
:root {
  --space: 1rem;
  --radius: 8px;
  --accent: #e34c26;
}
.card {
  padding: var(--space);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  border-top: 4px solid var(--accent);
}
```

Custom properties inherit and can be changed in a media query, which makes dark mode easy:

```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root { --bg: #111; --text: #eee; }
}
```

## Units

| Unit | Relative to | Good for |
|---|---|---|
| `px` | nothing (fixed) | borders, tiny details |
| `rem` | root font size | font sizes, spacing |
| `em` | element's font size | padding that scales with text |
| `%` | parent | widths |
| `vw` / `vh` | viewport | full-screen sections |
| `ch` | width of "0" | text line length |

`clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem)` gives a fluid size with a minimum and maximum.

## Typography

```css
body {
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
}
```

- Always end `font-family` with a generic family (`serif`, `sans-serif`, `monospace`).
- Web fonts can be loaded with `@font-face` or a service; offline apps should bundle the font files.
- `font-weight`: 400 normal, 700 bold.

