lessons.notes:
## The viewport tag

```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
```

Never disable zoom (`user-scalable=no`): it hurts accessibility.

## Fluid foundations

```css
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
img, video { max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
.container { width: min(100% - 2rem, 70rem); margin-inline: auto; }
```

Prefer `max-width`, `%`, `fr`, `minmax()` and flex-wrap over fixed widths.

## Media queries

```css
/* mobile first: base styles for small screens */
.nav { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }

@media (min-width: 48rem) {        /* about 768px */
  .nav { flex-direction: row; }
}
```

- Choose breakpoints where **your content** breaks, not for specific devices.
- Using `rem`/`em` in queries respects the user's font size.
- Range syntax works in modern browsers: `@media (width >= 48rem)`.

## User preference queries

```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --bg: #111; --text: #eee; } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; } }
```

## Responsive images

```html
<img src="photo-800.jpg"
     srcset="photo-400.jpg 400w, photo-800.jpg 800w, photo-1600.jpg 1600w"
     sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 50vw, 100vw"
     alt="Mountain lake at dawn">

<picture>
  <source srcset="hero.avif" type="image/avif">
  <img src="hero.jpg" alt="Team at work">
</picture>
```

## Container queries

```css
.sidebar, .main { container-type: inline-size; }
@container (min-width: 30rem) { .card { grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; } }
```

Components adapt to the space they get, wherever they are placed.

## Testing

Resize the preview, and use the device toolbar in browser developer tools. Check tap targets are at least about 44 by 44 pixels and text is readable without zooming.

